# Shell scripts MUST use LF line endings. bash fails with
# "syntax error near unexpected token" on CRLF (it reads `then\r` as a
# non-keyword, orphaning the following `elif`/`fi`). On Windows,
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check these out CRLF and break both the
# pre-push git hook and tests/test_pre_push_hook.py (PR-E2 #102b finding).
#
# Scoped to shell scripts only (not `* text=auto`) so this introduces no
# repo-wide renormalization — eol attributes apply to future checkouts, not
# retroactively.
*.sh        text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/** text eol=lf
